{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-34768","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52029","text":"TRAAVIIS — Serial Batch Closure"}]},{"id":"blk-34769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52030","marks":["bold"],"text":"Answers:"},{"id":"spn-52031","text":" the fourth GPT-5.6 ruling, "},{"id":"spn-52032","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"CLI wiring and `trvs compare` are accepted; close one remaining attestation defect, then build serial batch.\""}]},{"id":"blk-34770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52033","text":"Two things shipped, in the order the ruling required them:"}]},{"id":"blk-34771","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52034","text":"the "},{"id":"spn-52035","marks":["bold"],"text":"blocking closure"},{"id":"spn-52036","text":" — the dual-wiring and fabricable-"},{"id":"spn-52037","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_context"}]}],"id":"blk-34772","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-34774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52038","text":"defect in the direct "},{"id":"spn-52039","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_episodes"},{"id":"spn-52040","text":" API (checks "},{"id":"spn-52041","marks":["bold"],"text":"C15c–C15g"},{"id":"spn-52042","text":");"}]},{"id":"blk-34775","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52043","text":"the "},{"id":"spn-52044","marks":["bold"],"text":"serial candidate batch"},{"id":"spn-52045","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-52046","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs batch"},{"id":"spn-52047","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52048","marks":["code"],"text":"CandidateSetV1"},{"id":"spn-52049","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-34776","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-34778","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52050","marks":["code"],"text":"SerialBatchV1"},{"id":"spn-52051","text":" (battery "},{"id":"spn-52052","marks":["bold"],"text":"B1–B30"},{"id":"spn-52053","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-34779","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52054","text":"1. The blocking closure: "},{"id":"spn-52055","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_episodes"},{"id":"spn-52056","text":" attests only what replayed"}]},{"id":"blk-34780","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52057","text":"The ruling reproduced the defect directly. Supplying both "},{"id":"spn-52058","marks":["code"],"text":"registry="},{"id":"spn-52059","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-52060","marks":["code"],"text":"extra_verifiers="},{"id":"spn-52061","text":" replayed with the caller's implementations while the report claimed "},{"id":"spn-52062","marks":["code"],"text":"{\"wiring\": \"registry\", \"registry_version\": \"reg-v1\", …}"},{"id":"spn-52063","text":"; and "},{"id":"spn-52064","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_context="},{"id":"spn-52065","text":" could be handed in wholesale, with no relation to anything that ran."}]},{"id":"blk-34781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52066","text":"This is the same defect I had just fixed in "},{"id":"spn-52067","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_split"},{"id":"spn-52068","text":". I fixed "},{"id":"spn-52069","marks":["bold"],"text":"the instance, not the class"},{"id":"spn-52070","text":" — so the repair here is structural rather than a warning in a docstring."}]},{"id":"blk-34782","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52071","marks":["bold"],"text":"The shape of the fix."},{"id":"spn-52072","text":" One private seam, "},{"id":"spn-52073","marks":["code"],"text":"_wire(registry, extra_verifiers)"},{"id":"spn-52074","text":", returns "},{"id":"spn-52075","marks":["code"],"text":"(implementations, runtime_context)"},{"id":"spn-52076","text":" "},{"id":"spn-52077","marks":["bold"],"text":"together, from one branch"},{"id":"spn-52078","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-34783","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"if registry is not None and extra_verifiers is not None:\n    raise ComparisonError(\"VERIFIER_WIRING_AMBIGUOUS\", …)\n\nif extra_verifiers is not None:\n    return dict(extra_verifiers), _runtime_context(None)   # caller_supplied\n\n…\nreturn implementations, _runtime_context(registry)          # registry"},{"id":"blk-34784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52079","text":"There is no structure in which the report can describe a different runtime than the one that did the work, because the two values are produced by the same "},{"id":"spn-52080","marks":["code"],"text":"return"},{"id":"spn-52081","text":". The public "},{"id":"spn-52082","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_context="},{"id":"spn-52083","text":" parameter is "},{"id":"spn-52084","marks":["bold"],"text":"gone"},{"id":"spn-52085","text":": the only way to obtain an attestation is to perform the replay it describes. The signature is now exactly "},{"id":"spn-52086","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_episodes(left_dir, right_dir, *, registry=None, extra_verifiers=None)"},{"id":"spn-52087","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52088","text":"The CLI is unaffected — it only ever passed "},{"id":"spn-52089","marks":["code"],"text":"registry="},{"id":"spn-52090","text":", which is precisely why the defect went unnoticed and precisely why the fix had to be structural."}]},{"id":"blk-34786","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52091","text":"C15c–C15g"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34788","spans":[{"id":"spn-52092","text":"Check"}]},{"id":"blk-34789","spans":[{"id":"spn-52093","text":"Law"}]},{"id":"blk-34790","spans":[{"id":"spn-52094","text":"Result"}]}],"id":"blk-34787","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34791","spans":[{"id":"spn-52095","text":"C15c"}]},{"id":"blk-34792","spans":[{"id":"spn-52096","marks":["code"],"text":"registry="},{"id":"spn-52097","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-52098","marks":["code"],"text":"extra_verifiers="},{"id":"spn-52099","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-52100","marks":["code"],"text":"VERIFIER_WIRING_AMBIGUOUS"},{"id":"spn-52101","text":", nothing replayed"}]},{"id":"blk-34793","spans":[{"id":"spn-52102","text":"green"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34794","spans":[{"id":"spn-52103","text":"C15d"}]},{"id":"blk-34795","spans":[{"id":"spn-52104","text":"no "},{"id":"spn-52105","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_context"},{"id":"spn-52106","text":" parameter exists; passing one is a "},{"id":"spn-52107","marks":["code"],"text":"TypeError"},{"id":"spn-52108","text":"; signature is exact"}]},{"id":"blk-34796","spans":[{"id":"spn-52109","text":"green"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34797","spans":[{"id":"spn-52110","text":"C15e"}]},{"id":"blk-34798","spans":[{"id":"spn-52111","text":"a registry-supplied replay attests "},{"id":"spn-52112","marks":["italic"],"text":"that"},{"id":"spn-52113","text":" registry — both its version and its implementations"}]},{"id":"blk-34799","spans":[{"id":"spn-52114","text":"green"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34800","spans":[{"id":"spn-52115","text":"C15f"}]},{"id":"blk-34801","spans":[{"id":"spn-52116","text":"a caller-supplied replay always attests "},{"id":"spn-52117","marks":["code"],"text":"caller_supplied"},{"id":"spn-52118","text":", however registry-like the input"}]},{"id":"blk-34802","spans":[{"id":"spn-52119","text":"green"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34803","spans":[{"id":"spn-52120","text":"C15g"}]},{"id":"blk-34804","spans":[{"id":"spn-52121","text":"the CLI's "},{"id":"spn-52122","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-52123","text":" output is byte-identical to the library called with "},{"id":"spn-52124","marks":["code"],"text":"registry="}]},{"id":"blk-34805","spans":[{"id":"spn-52125","text":"green"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52126","marks":["bold"],"text":"One correction to my own first draft of C15e."},{"id":"spn-52127","text":" I initially proved \"the report names the registry you handed it\" by passing a registry with no "},{"id":"spn-52128","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-52129","text":" verifier and asserting "},{"id":"spn-52130","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-52131","text":" was absent from "},{"id":"spn-52132","marks":["code"],"text":"verifiers_available"},{"id":"spn-52133","text":". That test failed — and it "},{"id":"spn-52134","marks":["italic"],"text":"should"},{"id":"spn-52135","text":" have. These tasks declare "},{"id":"spn-52136","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-52137","text":", so a registry that cannot answer it cannot judge the bundle at all: the replay correctly refused with "},{"id":"spn-52138","marks":["code"],"text":"EPISODE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-52139","text":". There was never a report to inspect."}]},{"id":"blk-34807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52140","text":"The refusal is the stronger law, so C15e now proves both halves:"}]},{"id":"blk-34808","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52141","marks":["bold"],"text":"attestation"},{"id":"spn-52142","text":" — a registry carrying a version string no default could"}]}],"id":"blk-34809","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52143","text":"produce ("},{"id":"spn-52144","marks":["code"],"text":"…v1+compare-law-c15e"},{"id":"spn-52145","text":") must be quoted verbatim in the report;"}]},{"id":"blk-34812","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52146","marks":["bold"],"text":"implementations"},{"id":"spn-52147","text":" — a registry without "},{"id":"spn-52148","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-52149","text":" must make the replay"}]}],"id":"blk-34813","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52150","marks":["italic"],"text":"refuse"},{"id":"spn-52151","text":", while the default registry closes the same pair. A comparison that still appeared would have been judged by implementations nobody supplied."}]},{"id":"blk-34816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52152","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_compare.py"},{"id":"spn-52153","text":" is now "},{"id":"spn-52154","marks":["bold"],"text":"32 laws"},{"id":"spn-52155","text":", all green."}]},{"id":"blk-34817","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52156","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-52157","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs batch"},{"id":"spn-52158","text":" — the serial candidate-by-task matrix"}]},{"id":"blk-34818","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs batch PACKAGE SPLIT --candidates candidates.json --output batch-out [--json]"},{"id":"blk-34819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52159","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-52160","text":" is mandatory: comparisons replay "},{"id":"spn-52161","marks":["italic"],"text":"persisted"},{"id":"spn-52162","text":" closures."}]},{"id":"blk-34820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52163","text":"Built strictly as the composition the ruling specified — "},{"id":"spn-52164","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_split"},{"id":"spn-52165","text":" in one direction, "},{"id":"spn-52166","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-52167","text":" in the other, "},{"id":"spn-52168","marks":["bold"],"text":"no third mechanism underneath"},{"id":"spn-52169","text":". New module "},{"id":"spn-52170","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/batch.py"},{"id":"spn-52171","text":"; new CLI command "},{"id":"spn-52172","marks":["code"],"text":"cmd_batch"},{"id":"spn-52173","text":"; no change to "},{"id":"spn-52174","marks":["code"],"text":"evalone"},{"id":"spn-52175","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52176","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_bundle"},{"id":"spn-52177","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52178","marks":["code"],"text":"runner"},{"id":"spn-52179","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52180","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52181","text":", or the identity ladder."}]},{"id":"blk-34821","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52182","text":"Admission order, as ruled"}]},{"id":"blk-34822","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"open package + rederive env closure\n→ resolve split once\n→ admit shared subject once\n→ validate the complete CandidateSetV1\n→ construct one engine + registry\n→ create temporary output sibling\n→ run each candidate serially through eval_split\n→ persist and close each episode\n→ compare candidates task-by-task\n→ write SerialBatchV1\n→ atomically rename the output directory"},{"id":"blk-34823","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52183","text":"Nothing launches until the entire package, split and candidate set are admitted (B1, B1b). "},{"id":"spn-52184","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_split"},{"id":"spn-52185","text":" re-opens and re-admits per candidate; that is a per-candidate "},{"id":"spn-52186","marks":["italic"],"text":"re-check"},{"id":"spn-52187","text":", not a substitute for the preflight, and the preflight is what makes a typo in the fifth candidate cost zero agent runs."}]},{"id":"blk-34824","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52188","marks":["code"],"text":"CandidateSetV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34825","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"candidate_set_version\": \"traaviis.candidate-set.v1\",\n  \"candidates\": [{\"candidate_key\": \"repair\", \"argv\": [\"python3\", \"agent.py\", \"ok\"]}]\n}"},{"id":"blk-34826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52189","text":"Validated "},{"id":"spn-52190","marks":["bold"],"text":"whole, before anything runs"},{"id":"spn-52191","text":", with a distinct code per structural failure: "},{"id":"spn-52192","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_SET_MALFORMED"},{"id":"spn-52193","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52194","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_SET_VERSION"},{"id":"spn-52195","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52196","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_SET_EMPTY"},{"id":"spn-52197","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52198","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_KEY_INVALID"},{"id":"spn-52199","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52200","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_KEY_DUPLICATE"},{"id":"spn-52201","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52202","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_ARGV_INVALID"},{"id":"spn-52203","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52204","marks":["code"],"text":"CANDIDATE_SET_UNREADABLE"},{"id":"spn-52205","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52206","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-52207","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate_key"},{"id":"spn-52208","text":" is a report label "},{"id":"spn-52209","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-52210","text":" a directory name "},{"id":"spn-52211","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-52212","text":" half of a comparison filename, so it is constrained to what is unambiguous in all three roles: "},{"id":"spn-52213","marks":["code"],"text":"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}"},{"id":"spn-52214","text":", and it may not contain "},{"id":"spn-52215","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-52216","text":", the pair separator — otherwise "},{"id":"spn-52217","marks":["code"],"text":"a--b--c.json"},{"id":"spn-52218","text":" parses two ways."}]},{"id":"blk-34828","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52219","text":"Entries are "},{"id":"spn-52220","marks":["bold"],"text":"strict"},{"id":"spn-52221","text":": an unknown field is refused. That is not fastidiousness. An "},{"id":"spn-52222","marks":["code"],"text":"env"},{"id":"spn-52223","text":" key silently ignored would look like a way to give one candidate a different environment, which is the one thing a matrix must not permit (B4)."}]},{"id":"blk-34829","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52224","marks":["code"],"text":"SerialBatchV1"},{"id":"spn-52225","text":" and the published tree"}]},{"id":"blk-34830","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"batch-out/\n├── batch.json\n├── candidates/<key>/evaluation.json\n├── candidates/<key>/episodes/episode-…/\n└── comparisons/task-…/<left>--<right>.json"},{"id":"blk-34831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52226","text":"Every unordered pair once, in sorted-key direction. The whole tree is populated in a staging sibling and published by "},{"id":"spn-52227","marks":["bold"],"text":"one `os.replace`"},{"id":"spn-52228","text":" (B22): a reader never sees three of four candidates, and a failed batch leaves neither an output directory nor a staging directory behind (B23)."}]},{"id":"blk-34832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52229","marks":["code"],"text":"SerialBatchV1"},{"id":"spn-52230","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-52231","marks":["bold"],"text":"no id"},{"id":"spn-52232","text":". There is no "},{"id":"spn-52233","marks":["code"],"text":"batch-"},{"id":"spn-52234","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52235","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate-"},{"id":"spn-52236","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52237","marks":["code"],"text":"agent-"},{"id":"spn-52238","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-52239","marks":["code"],"text":"compare-"},{"id":"spn-52240","text":" prefix anywhere in the report or in any filename (B19)."}]},{"id":"blk-34833","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52241","text":"The three properties that make the matrix mean something"}]},{"id":"blk-34834","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52242","marks":["bold"],"text":"One environment, one subject, one registry."},{"id":"spn-52243","text":" Every candidate answers"}]}],"id":"blk-34835","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52244","text":"byte-identical "},{"id":"spn-52245","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-52246","text":" bytes over one admitted subject, judged by one "},{"id":"spn-52247","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"},{"id":"spn-52248","text":" that both "},{"id":"spn-52249","marks":["italic"],"text":"ran"},{"id":"spn-52250","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-52251","marks":["italic"],"text":"replayed"},{"id":"spn-52252","text":" every episode. Every "},{"id":"spn-52253","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1"},{"id":"spn-52254","text":" and every "},{"id":"spn-52255","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-52256","text":" attests that same registry (B7–B9)."}]},{"id":"blk-34838","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34840","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52257","marks":["bold"],"text":"Comparisons replay; they do not trust the run that just happened."},{"id":"spn-52258","text":" Each"}]}],"id":"blk-34839","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52259","text":"pair reopens both persisted bundles through "},{"id":"spn-52260","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_episodes"},{"id":"spn-52261","text":", which reverifies each side to "},{"id":"spn-52262","marks":["code"],"text":"closed"},{"id":"spn-52263","text":" first. No agent is launched during the comparison half (B28)."}]},{"id":"blk-34842","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52264","marks":["bold"],"text":"A refusal is recorded, not smoothed over."},{"id":"spn-52265","text":" A pair with a missing side"}]}],"id":"blk-34843","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52266","text":"yields a typed refusal naming both candidates — never a fabricated relation, and no member written to disk (B14)."}]},{"id":"blk-34846","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52267","text":"3. Three defects found while building, and closed"}]},{"id":"blk-34847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52268","text":"None was in the ruling. The first two were found by writing the laws; the third by running the release gate wrong."}]},{"id":"blk-34848","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52269","text":"(a) A missing agent binary aborted the whole run"}]},{"id":"blk-34849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52270","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_split"},{"id":"spn-52271","text":" caught "},{"id":"spn-52272","marks":["code"],"text":"AdmissionError"},{"id":"spn-52273","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-52274","marks":["code"],"text":"UnsupportedPolicyError"},{"id":"spn-52275","text":" around "},{"id":"spn-52276","marks":["code"],"text":"evalone.evaluate"},{"id":"spn-52277","text":", but not "},{"id":"spn-52278","marks":["code"],"text":"OSError"},{"id":"spn-52279","text":". The most ordinary way an agent fails is that "},{"id":"spn-52280","marks":["code"],"text":"argv[0]"},{"id":"spn-52281","text":" does not exist, and "},{"id":"spn-52282","marks":["code"],"text":"subprocess"},{"id":"spn-52283","text":" raises "},{"id":"spn-52284","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-52285","text":" for that — which escaped, abandoning every remaining task in the split over one caller's typo. Once several candidates share a split it abandoned every remaining "},{"id":"spn-52286","marks":["bold"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-52287","text":" too, which would have made B15 unsatisfiable."}]},{"id":"blk-34850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52288","text":"An agent that cannot be launched is a result for that task, exactly like one that ran and failed. "},{"id":"spn-52289","marks":["code"],"text":"OSError"},{"id":"spn-52290","text":" is now caught and recorded."}]},{"id":"blk-34851","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52291","text":"(b) \"No bundle\" conflated a candidate failure with a write failure"}]},{"id":"blk-34852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52292","text":"Two very different events both leave a cell without a bundle:"}]},{"id":"blk-34853","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52293","text":"the "},{"id":"spn-52294","marks":["bold"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-52295","text":" produced nothing to keep — a comparison refusal, the batch"}]}],"id":"blk-34854","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52296","text":"continues, exit stays 0;"}]},{"id":"blk-34857","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52297","text":"the "},{"id":"spn-52298","marks":["bold"],"text":"batch"},{"id":"spn-52299","text":" could not write what it was handed (read-only output, full"}]}],"id":"blk-34858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52300","text":"disk) — infrastructure, abort, no output directory, exit 2."}]},{"id":"blk-34861","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52301","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1"},{"id":"spn-52302","text":"'s persistence block carried only "},{"id":"spn-52303","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-52304","text":" and an English "},{"id":"spn-52305","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-52306","text":" string, so a consumer had to match on prose to tell them apart. It now carries a machine-readable "},{"id":"spn-52307","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence.reason"},{"id":"spn-52308","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-52309","marks":["code"],"text":"no_episode"},{"id":"spn-52310","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52311","marks":["code"],"text":"no_artifacts"},{"id":"spn-52312","text":", "},{"id":"spn-52313","marks":["code"],"text":"write_failed"},{"id":"spn-52314","text":" — and "},{"id":"spn-52315","marks":["code"],"text":"batch"},{"id":"spn-52316","text":" branches on that. The prose is unchanged and still there."}]},{"id":"blk-34862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52317","text":"This is an "},{"id":"spn-52318","marks":["bold"],"text":"additive"},{"id":"spn-52319","text":" field on "},{"id":"spn-52320","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1"},{"id":"spn-52321","text":". The one behavioural change is that a task which failed to evaluate while "},{"id":"spn-52322","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-52323","text":" was requested now reports "},{"id":"spn-52324","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence.status = \"unavailable\""},{"id":"spn-52325","text":" (reason "},{"id":"spn-52326","marks":["code"],"text":"no_episode"},{"id":"spn-52327","text":") rather than "},{"id":"spn-52328","marks":["code"],"text":"\"not_requested\""},{"id":"spn-52329","text":"; the old value said nothing had been asked for, which was false. Neither "},{"id":"spn-52330","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence_closed"},{"id":"spn-52331","text":" nor "},{"id":"spn-52332","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence_error"},{"id":"spn-52333","text":" moves."}]},{"id":"blk-34863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52334","text":"Related: refusal "},{"id":"spn-52335","marks":["code"],"text":"detail"},{"id":"spn-52336","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-52337","marks":["code"],"text":"batch.json"},{"id":"spn-52338","text":" quotes the "},{"id":"spn-52339","marks":["bold"],"text":"reason code"},{"id":"spn-52340","text":", not the error message, because a launch failure's message names the argv that could not be launched — and an absolute host path in the index would make two identical batches on two machines differ (B20). The unabridged prose stays in that candidate's "},{"id":"spn-52341","marks":["code"],"text":"evaluation.json"},{"id":"spn-52342","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34864","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52343","text":"(c) The release gate blamed the packet for the operator's typo"}]},{"id":"blk-34865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52344","text":"Certifying this slice, I ran "},{"id":"spn-52345","marks":["code"],"text":"accept_packet.py --forge /tmp/gateforge"},{"id":"spn-52346","text":" against a path that did not exist. G6 ran the battery with "},{"id":"spn-52347","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVS_FORGE_DIR"},{"id":"spn-52348","text":" set to a non-directory, seven engine-dependent laws failed, one file crashed, and the tool printed "},{"id":"spn-52349","marks":["bold"],"text":"REJECTED"},{"id":"spn-52350","text":" and exited 1."}]},{"id":"blk-34866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52351","text":"Nothing was wrong with the packet. A missing forge dir does not make the engine "},{"id":"spn-52352","marks":["italic"],"text":"absent"},{"id":"spn-52353","text":" — G5 already covers absent, and covers it by asserting that the laws notice. It makes the engine "},{"id":"spn-52354","marks":["bold"],"text":"broken"},{"id":"spn-52355","text":", which no gate is written to interpret. The verdict named the packet for a mistake made by the harness invoking it."}]},{"id":"blk-34867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52356","text":"This is the same failure the ruling blocked on in "},{"id":"spn-52357","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_episodes"},{"id":"spn-52358","text":", one layer out: a report describing something other than what actually happened. The fix is the same shape — refuse rather than narrate. "},{"id":"spn-52359","marks":["code"],"text":"--forge"},{"id":"spn-52360","text":" is now checked before any gate runs, and the exit contract gains the third code the rest of the tree already uses:"}]},{"id":"blk-34868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52361","text":"0  every requested gate passed              ACCEPTED 1  a gate judged the packet and it failed   REJECTED 2  no verdict was reached; the harness was wrong"}]},{"id":"blk-34869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52362","text":"A missing packet file also moves from 1 to 2, for the same reason: not finding the archive is not a judgement about it."}]},{"id":"blk-34870","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52363","text":"4. Battery"}]},{"id":"blk-34871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52364","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_batch.py"},{"id":"spn-52365","text":" — 34 laws covering B1–B30, all green."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34873","spans":[{"id":"spn-52366","text":"Check"}]},{"id":"blk-34874","spans":[{"id":"spn-52367","text":"Required result"}]},{"id":"blk-34875","spans":[{"id":"spn-52368","text":"Where"}]}],"id":"blk-34872","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34876","spans":[{"id":"spn-52369","text":"B1"}]},{"id":"blk-34877","spans":[{"id":"spn-52370","text":"candidate set completely validated before any launch"}]},{"id":"blk-34878","spans":[{"id":"spn-52371","text":"B1, B1b"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34879","spans":[{"id":"spn-52372","text":"B2"}]},{"id":"blk-34880","spans":[{"id":"spn-52373","text":"duplicate or malformed candidate keys refused"}]},{"id":"blk-34881","spans":[{"id":"spn-52374","text":"B2, B2b"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34882","spans":[{"id":"spn-52375","text":"B3"}]},{"id":"blk-34883","spans":[{"id":"spn-52376","text":"commands are argv arrays, not shell strings"}]},{"id":"blk-34884","spans":[{"id":"spn-52377","text":"B3"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34885","spans":[{"id":"spn-52378","text":"B4"}]},{"id":"blk-34886","spans":[{"id":"spn-52379","text":"host environment not inherited into candidates"}]},{"id":"blk-34887","spans":[{"id":"spn-52380","text":"B4"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34888","spans":[{"id":"spn-52381","text":"B5"}]},{"id":"blk-34889","spans":[{"id":"spn-52382","text":"every candidate answers the same frozen task ids"}]},{"id":"blk-34890","spans":[{"id":"spn-52383","text":"B5"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34891","spans":[{"id":"spn-52384","text":"B6"}]},{"id":"blk-34892","spans":[{"id":"spn-52385","text":"execution order deterministic"}]},{"id":"blk-34893","spans":[{"id":"spn-52386","text":"B6"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34894","spans":[{"id":"spn-52387","text":"B7"}]},{"id":"blk-34895","spans":[{"id":"spn-52388","text":"exactly one registry instance serves the whole batch"}]},{"id":"blk-34896","spans":[{"id":"spn-52389","text":"B7"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34897","spans":[{"id":"spn-52390","text":"B8"}]},{"id":"blk-34898","spans":[{"id":"spn-52391","text":"every "},{"id":"spn-52392","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1"},{"id":"spn-52393","text":" attests that registry"}]},{"id":"blk-34899","spans":[{"id":"spn-52394","text":"B8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34900","spans":[{"id":"spn-52395","text":"B9"}]},{"id":"blk-34901","spans":[{"id":"spn-52396","text":"every "},{"id":"spn-52397","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-52398","text":" attests that registry"}]},{"id":"blk-34902","spans":[{"id":"spn-52399","text":"B9"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34903","spans":[{"id":"spn-52400","text":"B10"}]},{"id":"blk-34904","spans":[{"id":"spn-52401","text":"each candidate/task pair produces at most one episode"}]},{"id":"blk-34905","spans":[{"id":"spn-52402","text":"B10"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34906","spans":[{"id":"spn-52403","text":"B11"}]},{"id":"blk-34907","spans":[{"id":"spn-52404","text":"episodes retain their independently derived ids"}]},{"id":"blk-34908","spans":[{"id":"spn-52405","text":"B11"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34909","spans":[{"id":"spn-52406","text":"B12"}]},{"id":"blk-34910","spans":[{"id":"spn-52407","text":"all unordered candidate pairs considered per task"}]},{"id":"blk-34911","spans":[{"id":"spn-52408","text":"B12"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34912","spans":[{"id":"spn-52409","text":"B13"}]},{"id":"blk-34913","spans":[{"id":"spn-52410","text":"closed pairs receive deterministic "},{"id":"spn-52411","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-52412","text":" reports"}]},{"id":"blk-34914","spans":[{"id":"spn-52413","text":"B13"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34915","spans":[{"id":"spn-52414","text":"B14"}]},{"id":"blk-34916","spans":[{"id":"spn-52415","text":"unavailable pairs receive typed refusals, not fake comparisons"}]},{"id":"blk-34917","spans":[{"id":"spn-52416","text":"B14"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34918","spans":[{"id":"spn-52417","text":"B15"}]},{"id":"blk-34919","spans":[{"id":"spn-52418","text":"one candidate failure does not abandon later candidates"}]},{"id":"blk-34920","spans":[{"id":"spn-52419","text":"B14, B15b"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34921","spans":[{"id":"spn-52420","text":"B16"}]},{"id":"blk-34922","spans":[{"id":"spn-52421","text":"null reward remains incomparable"}]},{"id":"blk-34923","spans":[{"id":"spn-52422","text":"B16"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34924","spans":[{"id":"spn-52423","text":"B17"}]},{"id":"blk-34925","spans":[{"id":"spn-52424","text":"equal reward preserves trace differences"}]},{"id":"blk-34926","spans":[{"id":"spn-52425","text":"B17"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34927","spans":[{"id":"spn-52426","text":"B18"}]},{"id":"blk-34928","spans":[{"id":"spn-52427","text":"candidate labels enter no TRAAVIIS identity"}]},{"id":"blk-34929","spans":[{"id":"spn-52428","text":"B18"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34930","spans":[{"id":"spn-52429","text":"B19"}]},{"id":"blk-34931","spans":[{"id":"spn-52430","text":"no "},{"id":"spn-52431","marks":["code"],"text":"batch-"},{"id":"spn-52432","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-52433","marks":["code"],"text":"agent-"},{"id":"spn-52434","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-52435","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate-"},{"id":"spn-52436","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-52437","marks":["code"],"text":"compare-"},{"id":"spn-52438","text":" id appears"}]},{"id":"blk-34932","spans":[{"id":"spn-52439","text":"B19"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34933","spans":[{"id":"spn-52440","text":"B20"}]},{"id":"blk-34934","spans":[{"id":"spn-52441","text":"no absolute path or wall-clock timestamp in "},{"id":"spn-52442","marks":["code"],"text":"batch.json"}]},{"id":"blk-34935","spans":[{"id":"spn-52443","text":"B20"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34936","spans":[{"id":"spn-52444","text":"B21"}]},{"id":"blk-34937","spans":[{"id":"spn-52445","text":"output members use only relative deterministic paths"}]},{"id":"blk-34938","spans":[{"id":"spn-52446","text":"B21"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34939","spans":[{"id":"spn-52447","text":"B22"}]},{"id":"blk-34940","spans":[{"id":"spn-52448","text":"final output directory published atomically"}]},{"id":"blk-34941","spans":[{"id":"spn-52449","text":"B22, B22b"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34942","spans":[{"id":"spn-52450","text":"B23"}]},{"id":"blk-34943","spans":[{"id":"spn-52451","text":"failed batch leaves no final directory or partial index"}]},{"id":"blk-34944","spans":[{"id":"spn-52452","text":"B23"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34945","spans":[{"id":"spn-52453","text":"B24"}]},{"id":"blk-34946","spans":[{"id":"spn-52454","text":"two runs over equivalent evidence are byte-identical"}]},{"id":"blk-34947","spans":[{"id":"spn-52455","text":"B24"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34948","spans":[{"id":"spn-52456","text":"B25"}]},{"id":"blk-34949","spans":[{"id":"spn-52457","text":"honest repair outranks "},{"id":"spn-52458","marks":["code"],"text":"nofix"},{"id":"spn-52459","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-52460","marks":["code"],"text":"gutspec"},{"id":"spn-52461","text":" per task"}]},{"id":"blk-34950","spans":[{"id":"spn-52462","text":"B25"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34951","spans":[{"id":"spn-52463","text":"B26"}]},{"id":"blk-34952","spans":[{"id":"spn-52464","text":"task pairing never crosses task ids"}]},{"id":"blk-34953","spans":[{"id":"spn-52465","text":"B26"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34954","spans":[{"id":"spn-52466","text":"B27"}]},{"id":"blk-34955","spans":[{"id":"spn-52467","text":"agents run serially, never concurrently"}]},{"id":"blk-34956","spans":[{"id":"spn-52468","text":"B27"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34957","spans":[{"id":"spn-52469","text":"B28"}]},{"id":"blk-34958","spans":[{"id":"spn-52470","text":"comparing does not rerun candidate agents"}]},{"id":"blk-34959","spans":[{"id":"spn-52471","text":"B28"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34960","spans":[{"id":"spn-52472","text":"B29"}]},{"id":"blk-34961","spans":[{"id":"spn-52473","text":"comparison API ambiguity closure remains green"}]},{"id":"blk-34962","spans":[{"id":"spn-52474","text":"B29"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34963","spans":[{"id":"spn-52475","text":"B30"}]},{"id":"blk-34964","spans":[{"id":"spn-52476","text":"existing A, C, repair, replay and packet gates remain green"}]},{"id":"blk-34965","spans":[{"id":"spn-52477","text":"B30, B30b + full battery"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52478","text":"Some laws are proved by observing a seam rather than by reading an output, because that is the only place the claim is visible:"}]},{"id":"blk-34967","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52479","marks":["bold"],"text":"B1/B28"},{"id":"spn-52480","text":" patch "},{"id":"spn-52481","marks":["code"],"text":"runner.run_agent"},{"id":"spn-52482","text":" and assert it was never called — the only"}]}],"id":"blk-34968","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52483","text":"seam that crosses into an agent process."}]},{"id":"blk-34971","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52484","marks":["bold"],"text":"B7/B27"},{"id":"spn-52485","text":" patch "},{"id":"spn-52486","marks":["code"],"text":"evalsplit.eval_split"},{"id":"spn-52487","text":" to record the registry object identity"}]}],"id":"blk-34972","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52488","text":"and to detect re-entrance; serial execution is proved by no candidate's run beginning before the previous one's ended."}]},{"id":"blk-34975","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52489","marks":["bold"],"text":"B22"},{"id":"spn-52490","text":" patches "},{"id":"spn-52491","marks":["code"],"text":"os.replace"},{"id":"spn-52492","text":" and inspects the world *at the moment of"}]}],"id":"blk-34976","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52493","text":"publication*: the destination does not exist, and the staged tree is already complete."}]},{"id":"blk-34979","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52494","marks":["bold"],"text":"B18"},{"id":"spn-52495","text":" renames every candidate, reruns, and asserts every "},{"id":"spn-52496","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-"},{"id":"spn-52497","text":" is"}]}],"id":"blk-34980","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52498","text":"byte-identical — which is what \"a local label, not an identity\" has to mean."}]},{"id":"blk-34983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52499","text":"Two laws are guarded against being vacuous, because both could pass for the wrong reason: "},{"id":"spn-52500","marks":["bold"],"text":"B6"},{"id":"spn-52501","text":" asserts the fixture's declared order is "},{"id":"spn-52502","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-52503","text":" already sorted, and "},{"id":"spn-52504","marks":["bold"],"text":"B17"},{"id":"spn-52505","text":" asserts an equal-reward pair actually occurred."}]},{"id":"blk-34984","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52506","text":"Certified totals"}]},{"id":"blk-34985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52507","text":"Counts below are what the tools printed, not a hand count — the distinction that put "},{"id":"spn-52508","marks":["code"],"text":"accept_packet.py"},{"id":"spn-52509","text":" in the tree in the first place."}]},{"id":"blk-34986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52510","text":"python3 tools/run_battery.py                        exit 0"}]},{"id":"blk-34987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52511","text":"test_batch.py            34 passed   0 skipped   0 failed   (new) test_compare.py          32 passed   0 skipped   0 failed   (+5, C15c-C15g) ...23 further files ------------------------------------------------------------ 434 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed  (25 files)"}]},{"id":"blk-34988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52512","text":"Seven gates, against "},{"id":"spn-52513","marks":["code"],"text":"--forge /home/travis/ProjectAmp2/TRVM/forge"},{"id":"spn-52514","text":":"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34990","spans":[{"id":"spn-52515","text":"Gate"}]},{"id":"blk-34991","spans":[{"id":"spn-52516","text":"Result"}]}],"id":"blk-34989","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34992","spans":[{"id":"spn-52517","text":"G1 manifest well formed"}]},{"id":"blk-34993","spans":[{"id":"spn-52518","text":"ok — 111 entries, "},{"id":"spn-52519","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.packet-manifest.v1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34994","spans":[{"id":"spn-52520","text":"G2 manifest agrees with archive"}]},{"id":"blk-34995","spans":[{"id":"spn-52521","text":"ok — 111 members hashed, all match"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34996","spans":[{"id":"spn-52522","text":"G3 archive metadata canonical"}]},{"id":"blk-34997","spans":[{"id":"spn-52523","text":"ok — unix modes, fixed timestamps, sorted"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34998","spans":[{"id":"spn-52524","text":"G4 